      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CRIME OF PASSION (3) is going really well. She does get back into the field in her races but attacks the line. The mare did deserve to break that maiden at Tamworth and it was by a nice margin. Gets the inside to save ground and easy to fancy her. SUTTON STORM (1) is the other one going well. He also got a long way off them to win first up and then couldn't quite make up the ground at Dubbo. The added ground is probably what he needs. INTERRO (4) ran a decent race at Newcastle. Her form from the previous preparation was a bit up and down but maybe she is looking for this journey now. HETA (2) did very little at this track when resuming but it was over a lot shorter. Not an easy step up 450m. OLE MISS (5) should be ready now third up. Does have to find something.",
